# Units masked on piv, one per line. Mask, not disable: a disabled unit can still be started by a
# socket, a timer or a dependency. Units that do not exist on the board are skipped.
#
# This is namchain host-slim's list for piv (bench-results/host-slim-state-piv.txt), which had
# decayed: its files were gone and all of these were running again on 2026-09-26.
#
# Package maintenance that wakes up on its own. Updates happen when you choose, not mid-gig.
apt-daily.service
apt-daily.timer
apt-daily-upgrade.service
apt-daily-upgrade.timer
unattended-upgrades.service
man-db.timer
fwupd.service
fwupd-refresh.timer
motd-news.service
motd-news.timer
ubuntu-advantage.service
ua-reboot-cmds.service
apport.service
# cloud-init and snapd: first-boot provisioning and snap refreshes.
cloud-init-local.service
cloud-final.service
cloud-config.service
cloud-init-main.service
cloud-init-network.service
snapd.service
snapd.socket
snapd.seeded.service
snapd.apparmor.service
# Hardware and services a pedal doesn't have or need.
ModemManager.service
bluetooth.service
udisks2.service
multipathd.service
open-iscsi.service
NetworkManager-wait-online.service
# Logging: the journal, in RAM, is enough.
rsyslog.service
sysstat.service
#
# Deliberately NOT masked:
#   avahi-daemon       host-slim masked it, but it is what makes piv.local resolve for ljoss,
#                      which has no discovery (plan 1.3). It is inactive today; not started either.
#   docker, containerd, libvirt
#                      piv's other jobs. They live in system.slice and machine.slice, so they run
#                      on cores 0-1 with everything else. Stop them before a soak.
#   NetworkManager, wpa_supplicant, systemd-networkd
#                      WiFi is the way in; the same boot-time-fallback question as tib's.
#   namchain-realtime-tune.service
#                      namchain's: sets the governor and turns USB autosuspend off. Harmless
#                      beside pedal-tune, and the autosuspend half is worth keeping.
